diff --git a/build/madeira-d3d12/gen-tess-tables.py b/build/madeira-d3d12/gen-tess-tables.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ee59b6f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/build/madeira-d3d12/gen-tess-tables.py
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""ml1152: turn Apple's ir_tessellator_tables.h (metal_irconverter_runtime) into a C byte array.
+
+The converter's emulated hull stage reads the tessellator tables from the buffer bound at
+kIRRuntimeTessellatorTablesBindPoint (object/mesh buffer 7); the layout is what
+IRRuntimeLoadTessellatorTables writes: the 64x64x2 uint32 counts-and-offset table (32768 bytes)
+followed by the uint8 lookup table (701114 bytes). usage: gen-tess-tables.py <header> <out.h>
+"""
+import re, struct, sys
+src = re.sub(r"//[^\n]*", "", open(sys.argv[1]).read())   # the lookup table carries "// in:N out:M" comments
+def array(name):
+    m = re.search(name + r'[^=]*=\s*\{(.*?)\n\};', src, re.S)
+    return [int(x) for x in re.findall(r'\d+', m.group(1))]
+counts = array('kIRTessellatorTablesCountsAndOffset')
+lookup = array('kIRTessellatorTablesLookupTable')
+assert len(counts) == 64 * 64 * 2, len(counts)
+blob = struct.pack('<%dI' % len(counts), *counts) + bytes(lookup)
+m = re.search(r'kIRRuntimeTessellatorTablesLookupTableLength\s*=\s*(\d+)', src)
+assert len(lookup) == int(m.group(1)), (len(lookup), m.group(1))
+with open(sys.argv[2], 'w') as f:
+    f.write('/* generated by gen-tess-tables.py from ir_tessellator_tables.h; do not edit */\n')
+    f.write('static const unsigned int mad_tess_tables_len = %du;\n' % len(blob))
+    f.write('static const unsigned char mad_tess_tables[] = {\n')
+    for i in range(0, len(blob), 32):
+        f.write(','.join(str(b) for b in blob[i:i+32]) + ',\n')
+    f.write('};\n')
+print('tessellator tables: %d + %d = %d bytes' % (len(counts) * 4, len(lookup), len(blob)))
diff --git a/docs/MACOS_X86_64.md b/docs/MACOS_X86_64.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c6854d2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/MACOS_X86_64.md
@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+# Building the D3D12 runtime for x86_64 macOS Wine
+
+Status 2026-10-12: builds; `d3d12-m2-x64.exe` 90/90, `d3d12-vfetch-x64.exe` 31/31,
+`d3d12-cube-x64.exe` presents, inside a stock x86_64 Wine 10 (Sikarugir / Porting Kit
+wrapper) on an M2 Pro, macOS 27.
+
+This is the same runtime that ships in the iOS app, built for the other shape of Wine:
+x86_64 PE modules under Rosetta, a Mach-O `winemetal.so` unixlib instead of the static
+archive linked into the app, no FEX, no remote Metal.
+
+## Inputs
+
+| Path (relative to the repo)                             | What                                                                                         |
+| -------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `toolchains/llvm-mingw-20260421-ucrt-macos-universal`    | the pinned llvm-mingw (docs/BUILDING.md)                                                     |
+| `toolchains/llvm-darwin`                                 | LLVM 15.0.7 static libraries built for x86_64 as in `dxmt/configure.sh` (the `llvm-darwin` block) |
+| `toolchains/wine`                                        | a Wine SDK with `bin/winebuild`, `lib/wine/x86_64-windows/lib{winecrt0,ntdll,dbghelp}.a` and `lib/wine/x86_64-unix/{ntdll,winemac}.so`; 3Shain's `wine.tar.gz` (v8.16-3shain) is what upstream DXMT's CI uses |
+| `dxmt/toolchains -> ../toolchains`                       | the dxmt cross files resolve `@GLOBAL_SOURCE_ROOT@/toolchains/...`                           |
+| `research/GPTK/Metal Shader Converter 4.0 beta 2.pkg`    | hash-checked by `build/madeira-d3d12/deps.sh`; its macOS universal dylib ships next to winemetal.so |
+| Xcode Metal toolchain                                    | `xcodebuild -downloadComponent MetalToolchain` (Xcode 26+ ships without it)                  |
+
+## Build
+
+```sh
+bash build/madeira-d3d12/build-macos-x86_64.sh
+```
+
+Steps, each of which can be run by hand:
+
+1. `meson setup dxmt/build-x86_64 dxmt --cross-file dxmt/build-x86_64-win.txt --native-file dxmt/build-osx.txt
+   -Dbuildtype=release -Dwine_install_path=<abs toolchains/wine> -Dnative_llvm_path=<abs toolchains/llvm-darwin>
+   -Dmadeira_d3d12_path=<abs madeira-d3d12> -Dmadeira_msc_include=<converter headers> -Dmadeira_converter_id=<hash>`
+2. `ninja -C dxmt/build-x86_64 src/winemetal/winemetal.dll src/winemetal/winemetal.dll.postproc src/winemetal/unix/winemetal.so`
+   (`postproc` runs `winebuild --builtin`, which is what lets ntdll find `winemetal.so`).
+   The same ninja call builds `src/dxgi/dxgi.dll`.
+3. `MADEIRA_PE_ARCH=x86_64 bash build/madeira-d3d12/build-pe.sh` for `d3d12.dll`,
+   `madeira_d3d12.dll`, `d3d12core.dll` and the three test executables.
+
+Output: `build/madeira-d3d12/out-macos/`.
+
+## Install into a Wine tree
+
+| File                                  | Goes to                                                     |
+| ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `winemetal.dll`                       | `lib/wine/x86_64-windows/` (replaces any stub of that name) |
+| `winemetal.so`, `libmetalirconverter.dylib` | `lib/wine/x86_64-unix/` (the converter is looked up next to winemetal.so) |
+| `d3d12.dll`, `d3d12core.dll`, `dxgi.dll` | the application folder, with `dxgi,d3d12,d3d12core=n,b` overrides (the swapchain is created through DXMT's dxgi, which asks the queue for IMTLDXGIDevice) |
+| test EXEs + `madeira_d3d12.dll`       | any folder; the tests load `madeira_d3d12.dll` by name      |
+
+`madeira.cfg` is read from `$HOME/Documents/madeira.cfg` of the Wine process.
+
+## What differs from the iOS build, and why
+
+- `dxmt/src/winemetal/unix/meson.build` compiles the converter service
+  (`madeira_ir_unix.mm`, `madeira_sm5_ia.cpp`, `madeira_ags.cpp`) into `winemetal.so` behind
+  `-Dmadeira_d3d12_path`; on iOS `build/dxmt-ios/build.sh` compiles the same files into the
+  app's static library. The ObjC++ archive changes meson's link driver for the .so, so the
+  target adds `-arch x86_64` itself.
+- `dxmt/src/winemetal/unix/wmt_macos_stubs.c` gives no-op bodies to the `ios_*` hooks that
+  the iOS app provides.
+- `os_proc_available_memory()` does not exist on macOS; `winemetal_unix.c` returns 0 there,
+  the value the budget code already treats as "limit unknown".
+- `madeira_ir_unix.mm` looks for the converter next to its own image before the app bundle.
+- `air_tessellation.metal`: `atomic_fetch_add_explicit` on a `threadgroup atomic_int *`, as
+  upstream 3Shain/dxmt; the private intrinsic changed arity in the Xcode 27 Metal toolchain.
+- `WMT_TRACE_RENDER=1` prints every render pass, viewport, scissor, rasterizer state, PSO
+  descriptor and draw from `winemetal.so`.
+
+## Test fixes that came out of this
+
+The tests zeroed their D3D12 descriptors and relied on defaults D3D12 does not have: a zero
+`RenderTargetWriteMask` writes nothing, a zeroed `DepthStencilState` does not depth-test, a
+zero `Shader4ComponentMapping` is "component 0 in every channel", and `Queue::Signal` is
+asynchronous. The runtime maps all of these faithfully (`mad_write_mask`, ml1061), which is
+why `vfetch_test.c`, which sets them, passed first and `m2_abi.c` and `cube_window.c` did not.
+Both now set them.
+
+## Running a game (Pioneers of Pagonia, 2026-10-12)
+
+- `MADEIRA_DOCS_DIR=<dir>` points the runtime at `<dir>/madeira.cfg` (any Wine process).
+- The video memory budget on macOS is Metal's recommended working set (`vram-mb` overrides); the
+  iOS jetsam formula reported 1024 MB here and the engine requires 1.5 GB.
+- `MakeResident`/`Evict` answer S_OK (the engine quits on E_NOTIMPL).
+- A texture asking for more mip levels than its size allows is clamped to the full chain, and views
+  past the clamp map to the last level (Metal asserts on both; the engine quits on E_INVALIDARG).
+- `MADEIRA_D3D12_TRACE_CAPS=1` logs every `CheckFeatureSupport` query and device `QueryInterface`.
+
